        <mxCell id="c49" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#b3a14d;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=8;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;" value="&lt;b&gt;Choosing a loopback mode&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Internal (RTL):&lt;/b&gt; first bring-up and regression — no wiring, deterministic, isolates the CDR from analog effects. Keep OBUFDS driving the pins so the scope can still probe tx_p / tx_n.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;External (off-chip):&lt;/b&gt; the real measurement — LVDS buffers, wire ISI and noise are in the loop; used for the BER, jitter-tolerance and power numbers.&lt;br&gt;• Both modes share one oscillator, so any frequency offset must come from the M4 jitter injector (TX MMCM phase ramp).&lt;br&gt;• Add &lt;b&gt;cfg_loopback&lt;/b&gt; to the I5 test-configuration interface (1 bit)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="1060" x="40" y="1360" as="geometry" />
